      },
      "text": {
        "content": "<h1>Phase 2 &mdash; Player Handouts</h1><p><em>Seven sheets. Every one of them also appears inline in the scene journal where it is found, but those pages carry GM text &mdash; do not share those. Share from here.</em></p><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Handout</th><th>Show it when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>The charts from Haskur&rsquo;s map-case</td><td>Scene 1, item 8. Leave it up for the rest of the review &mdash; the three roads east are on it, and so is the roadhouse they have not asked about yet.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>The false letter of passage</td><td>Scene 1, item 2, once someone has looked closely.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>The vellum strip</td><td>Scene 1, item 5, the moment the tube is opened. Four words. Let them sit with it.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>The ledger fragment</td><td>Scene 1, item 6.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>The locket miniature</td><td>Scene 3b, if they find the locket behind the framed sketch.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Gilst&rsquo;s note</td><td>Scene 3b, folded behind the portrait. Show it after the locket, not with it.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>The Sparrow fold</td><td>Scene 3d, however the chase ends. They get this one whether or not they catch her.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>The one thing not drawn.</strong> The <em>&quot;R.&quot;</em> on Handout 1 is deliberately not inked. When the Investigation DC 14 lands, put your finger on the sheet south of Loftwick and say where it is. Players and GM reading the same map is the point; a hunt for a mark that was never drawn is not.</p>",
        "format": 1,
        "markdown": null
      }
    },
    {
      "_id": "BR2P2HoPgCharts",
      "_key": "!journal.pages!BR2P2HandoutsJrnl.BR2P2HoPgCharts",
      "name": "Handout 1 — The Charts from Haskur's Map-Case",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": false,
        "level": 1
      },
      "sort": 200000,
      "ownership": {
        "default": 1
      },
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null,
        "duplicateSource": null,
        "exportSource": null,
        "coreVersion": "13.351",
        "systemId": "dnd5e",
        "systemVersion": "5.3.0",
        "createdTime": null,
        "modifiedTime": null,
        "lastModifiedBy": null
      },
      "text": {
        "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"modules/blooming-rot-2/assets/handouts/caravan-charts-trade-routes.jpg\" alt=\"A weathered, scorch-edged chart of the Sheldomar and the Woolly Bay: the Yeomanry and Loftwick at the southwest, Keoland and the Ulek states through the centre, Hardby and the Wild Coast on the eastern bay, with dashed trade routes running overland and by sea across the Azure Sea and the Sea of Gearnat.\" style=\"max-width: 100%; border-radius: 4px;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: center; font-style: italic; color: #6b5b3c; font-size: 0.95em;\">Three charts out of a brass tube. A printed sea chart, a printed road chart, and this &mdash; drawn by hand, on good vellum, by a man who kept asking how you move a thing from the eastern shore to here.</p>",
        "format": 1,
        "markdown": null
      }
    },
